An ancient argument.  The usual line is that "everyone who" implies that th=
ere is someone who and "anyone who" does not.  There is another, barely min=
ority, side that denies any such difference at all.  Those who hold that th=
ere is no difference are also divided about whether the no difference has o=
r lacks existential import. Lojban is split along those lines pretty sharpl=
y and I don't off hand know who is ahead at the moment (xorxes is of the no=
 difference school, as far as I remember, and no import; I am of the other)
 I would translate "anyone who" as 'ro da ganai da ... gi...' and "everyone=
 who" and 'ro da poi'; xorxes would probably take these to be equivalent, a=
long with a variety of things involving 'lo'.




